==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Zoge]]s spawn after 5.33 seconds<sup>160f</sup>, delay 23.33~30 seconds<sup>700f~900f</sup>.
*1 [[Diabrollow]] spawns after 10.67 seconds<sup>320f</sup>.
*1 [[Prof. Owlbrowley]] spawns after 26.67 seconds<sup>800f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Oldstrich]] spawns as the boss.
**1 [[Tarsiriel]] spawns after 13.33 seconds<sup>400f</sup>.
**3 [[Prof. Owlbrowley]]s spawn, delay 60~66.67 seconds<sup>1,800f~2,000f</sup>.
**3 [[Diabrollow]]s spawn after 33.33 seconds<sup>1,000f</sup>, delay 53.33~60 seconds<sup>1,600f~1,800f</sup>.

==Strategy==
This is a decently hard Oldstrich stage with Diabrollow, Prof. Owlbrowley and Tarsiriel as the main support. Since this stage is on base hit, you can use the starting enemies to build up your wallet. When you hit the base, use [[Talents|Talented]] [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]] to get his Explosion to chip the first Owlbrowley. Once that's done, lure Oldstrich and spam your anti-Zombie units like Talented [[Li'l Tank Cat (Special Cat)|Li'l Eraser Cat]], [[Wushu Cat (Rare Cat)|Shigong Cat]], and [[Vaulter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Housewife Cat]], while you use units like [[Kotatsu Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Octopus Cat]], [[Master Uril (Special Cat)|Esoteric Uril]], [[Phantom Cat (Rare Cat)|Bubble Cat]], and [[Master of Life Dr. Nova (Special Cat)|Master of Life Dr. Nova]] to deal with the supporting enemies.

==Trivia==
*The word 藻屑 ''mokuzu'' in Jetsam Lookout's Japanese name (藻屑みはらし台 ''Mokuzu Miharashidai'', "Seaweed Scrap Observation Platform"), literally translates to "seaweed scrap", but can also be used as a metaphor for death at sea, which may be why it contains [[:Category:Zombie Enemies|Zombies]].
*Jetsam Lookout and [[Renovated Shipwreck]] are typical [[Zero Legends]] stages, in contrast to how [[Floating Bus Stop]] and [[Ink Museum]] are designed like late [[Stories of Legend]] stages and [[Coral Housing]] and [[Kelp Campsite]] are designed like [[Uncanny Legends]] stages.

